<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Connecting the hole is the one the player presses most, and the only one with a short
       cooldown. The hole itself is permanent and free; somewhere for it to lead is not. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_InvoluteVent</defName>
    <label>vent</label>
    <description>Connect the hole. For half a minute anything striking the part it sits in arrives inside the volume instead of landing on the carrier - a share of incoming fire rather than a shield, since RimWorld picks where a blow lands by body coverage.\n\nWhile it is connected the carrier can fold through it, put people through it, and post things into it.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Darkvision</iconPath>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <cooldownTicksRange>2500</cooldownTicksRange>
    <targetRequired>false</targetRequired>
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>false</casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>true</sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>-1</range>
      <warmupTime>0.5</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_AbilityVent" />
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

  <!-- Going in leaves the hole standing where the carrier was. Coming back out lands them
       exactly there, which is the pressure the ability never stops applying. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_InvoluteFold</defName>
    <label>fold</label>
    <description>Step through the hole and out of the world, leaving a visible aperture where the carrier was standing. Cast again from inside to return to it, carrying one item or one downed person.\n\nAnything fired into the aperture arrives inside the volume, still travelling; collapse is what closes it.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Unstoppable</iconPath>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <cooldownTicksRange>2500</cooldownTicksRange>
    <targetRequired>false</targetRequired>
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>false</casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>true</sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>-1</range>
      <warmupTime>1</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_AbilityFold" />
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

  <!-- Deliberately not enemies-only. One rule - a pawn goes in - and it means something
       completely different depending on who it is pointed at. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_InvoluteSwallow</defName>
    <label>swallow</label>
    <description>Put someone into the volume - a raider in the carrier's face, or a colonist bleeding out across the field. They are neither hurt nor healed by it, only somewhere else.\n\nThe hole is hand-sized, so a person barely fits and nothing larger than a megaspider does; someone who went in downed can be carried out, but someone who walked in on their own feet cannot be picked up at all.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_PiercingSpine</iconPath>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <!-- Three in-game hours rather than a day. What pays for that is maxSwallowBodySize on the
         gene, not the clock: a size cap stops this being a delete key aimed at a diabolus and
         leaves the rescue alone, which a long cooldown did neither of. -->
    <cooldownTicksRange>7500</cooldownTicksRange>
    <!-- Not hostile. It deals no damage and it is meant to be pointed at your own people as
         often as at theirs - marking it hostile makes the game treat casting it on a colonist
         as an attack, which is the opposite of the rescue this ability exists for. -->
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>false</casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>true</sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>9.9</range>
      <warmupTime>3</warmupTime>
      <requireLineOfSight>true</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
        <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
        <canTargetMechs>true</canTargetMechs>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetLocations>false</canTargetLocations>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_AbilitySwallow" />
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

  <!-- What makes the volume somewhere worth arriving at. Minified furniture is an item. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_InvolutePost</defName>
    <label>post</label>
    <description>Push an item through the hole - medicine, food, a minified bed - and it stays in the volume until somebody carries it back out by hand. Works through the hole on the carrier's body while connected, or through a standing aperture from anywhere on the map.\n\nThis is what makes the volume somewhere to take a wounded colonist rather than a hole to die in.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_RobustDigestion</iconPath>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <cooldownTicksRange>1200</cooldownTicksRange>
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>false</casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>false</sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>15.9</range>
      <warmupTime>0.5</warmupTime>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
        <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetItems>true</canTargetItems>
        <thingCategory>Item</thingCategory>
        <mapObjectTargetsMustBeAutoAttackable>false</mapObjectTargetsMustBeAutoAttackable>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_AbilityPost" />
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

  <!-- Outside only, which is the one line that keeps it from being an accident. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_InvoluteCollapse</defName>
    <label>collapse</label>
    <description>End the volume. Everything in it goes - what was stored, what was built, whoever was put in there, and every round the hole has ever taken.\n\nA new fold opens a new empty room, so swallowing something and then collapsing kills it outright, at the cost of the carrier's entire dimension.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_MajorCellInstability</iconPath>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <cooldownTicksRange>60000</cooldownTicksRange>
    <targetRequired>false</targetRequired>
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>false</casterMustBeCapableOfViolence>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>true</sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>
    <confirmationDialogText>Everything inside the volume will be destroyed, including anything and anyone stored there. This cannot be undone.</confirmationDialogText>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>-1</range>
      <warmupTime>3</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_AbilityCollapse" />
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

</Defs>
